id: divine-roar
name: Divine Roar
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/encounter
# A God Maneuver: open where an effect grants it, only in God Ki, its 4(bT) paid in Divine Ki Points (maneuvers.mjs
# whyNotGod, spendManeuverCost). Who is within its Destructive Sphere (centered on you) is asked, the ones beside you
# ticked and the rest the table's (use-maneuver.mjs askHide); a Might Clash against each (chat.mjs postDivineRoar). Won:
# Guard Down and Impediment until the end of your next turn - and a Minion is Defeated, unless a Special Minion, which the
# system cannot tell apart, so the card says it.
godManeuver: true
divineRoar: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A God Maneuver: a Might Clash against everyone in a Destructive Sphere around you - won, Guard Down and Impediment until
  the end of your next turn, and a Minion Defeated.
text: >
  Divine Roar [1/Encounter]: You let out a holy war cry, bringing mortals to their knees in awe of your might.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –DKP Cost: 4(bT)
  –Effect: Make a Might Clash against all Characters within a Destructive Sphere AoE (centered on you). If you win, the
  losing Character(s) gain the Guard Down and Impediment Combat Conditions until the end of your next turn. If that
  Opponent is a Minion (except a Special Minion), they are Defeated.
